coder › Implemented `RateLimiter` as a token bucket in `src/limiter.ts` and added tests in `src/limiter.test.ts`.

What changed:
- Bucket starts full with `capacity` tokens; last refill time is captured from the injected `now()` at construction.
- `tryTake(n)` refuses immediately when `n > capacity`, otherwise lazily refills, then deducts `n` only if enough tokens exist and returns `false` without deducting otherwise.
- `available` lazily refills up to the current time and returns the (possibly fractional) token count.
- Refill is computed as `elapsedMs / 1000 * refillPerSecond` and capped at `capacity`.

Tests added:
- starts full
- take-nothing on insufficient tokens
- refuses `n > capacity` even when full
- continuous refill over time
- never refills past capacity
- fractional `available`
- fractional `tryTake`

